      "content": "Opposition to transgender women in women's sports often centers on the belief that male-to-female transgender athletes still possess enhanced physical traits (such as high muscle mass or bone density) that provide unfair advantages compared to cisgender women due to male testosterone exposure during development. In response, pro-inclusion advocates argue that current hormone replacement therapy (HRT) effectively neutralizes these biological differences and that gender identity should be the primary criterion for sports eligibility to foster inclusivity. The debate also frequently reaches a stalemate when the scientific community presents conflicting data regarding the exact magnitude and longevity of these physiological advantages after HRT is initiated.",
